---
import CodeBlock from './CodeBlock.astro';

// GitHub serves the newest release's assets under /releases/latest/download/,
// so these links follow every release without an edit here.
const latest = 'https://github.com/sylvainHellin/mailypoppins/releases/latest/download';
---

<section id="download" class="start" aria-labelledby="start-heading">
  <div class="content-wide">
    <header class="start-head">
      <h2 id="start-heading">Get started</h2>
    </header>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step">
        <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Install</h3>
          <div class="options">
            <div class="option">
              <p>The Mac app runs on Apple silicon, includes <code>mp</code> and updates itself.</p>
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${latest}/mailypoppins-desktop-aarch64-apple-darwin.dmg`}>Download .dmg</a>
              <p class="note">The app is not signed yet, so macOS asks you to allow it once in System Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security. <a href="/getting-started/#mac-app">The guide shows how</a>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="option">
              <p>Homebrew installs the terminal app and the command line on macOS and Linux:</p>
              <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`brew tap sylvainHellin/mailypoppins\nbrew install mailypoppins`} />
              <p class="note">
                You can also download a binary for
                <a href={`${latest}/mailypoppins-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz`}>macOS arm64</a>,
                <a href={`${latest}/mailypoppins-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz`}>Linux x86_64</a> or
                <a href={`${latest}/mailypoppins-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz`}>Linux x86_64 static</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Add an account</h3>
          <p>The Mac app asks for one on first launch. In a terminal, run <code>mp config init</code>. Any IMAP provider works, and so does Microsoft 365.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="step">
        <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Open your mail</h3>
          <p>Open the Mac app, or run <code>mp</code> for the terminal app. The first sync starts on its own.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p class="more"><a href="/getting-started/">Read the full guide</a> for signatures, drafts and sending.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .start {
    padding: var(--space-16) 0 var(--space-20);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
  }

  .start-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .start-head h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    font-size: 2rem;
  }

  .lead {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }

  .steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  .step + .step {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
  }

  .step-num {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 2.25rem;
    height: 2.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-cta);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .step-body h3 {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 var(--space-2);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }

  .step-body p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .options {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-10);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .option {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .option :global(.code-block) {
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .note {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted) !important;
  }

  .more {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 0;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .options {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-6);
    }

    .step {
      grid-template-columns: 2.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-3);
    }

    .start-head h2 {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
